      "## Boundaries have to survive other people",
      "This is where most attempts fall apart. It is easy to decide you will not check work messages after six. It is much harder when your boss messages at 4:53pm on a Friday and you can see the three dots.",
      "A boundary that only works when nobody tests it is not a boundary, it is a preference. The useful version is decided in advance, in specific terms, and it accounts for the fact that other people will push on it \u2014 not because they are villains, but because they have their own Friday going on.",
      "## Focus is a muscle you have not used in a while",
