      "Rules do exist. Europe has its data regulation, California has its own. They are aimed at an industry of data brokers built specifically to be hard to see into, which makes it an uphill fight \u2014 and it is being fought on behalf of your double rather than you.",
      "## Invented doubles now outperform real people",
      "The creator economy started with accidental celebrities in messy bedrooms explaining knitting patterns and reviewing video games badly. People trusted them precisely because there was obviously nothing behind it \u2014 no budget, no crew, no angle.",
      "It is now a corporate hierarchy. Brands spend serious money on small local accounts for one reason: those accounts still have the asset that famous people have spent, which is looking like a person instead of a billboard.",
      "Meanwhile, entirely computer-generated influencers have built substantial followings, signed deals with fashion labels and released music, while never having existed at all. The audience knows. It works anyway.",
      "That is the whole argument compressed into a single fact. People say they want authenticity. What they actually respond to is a convincing performance of it \u2014 and a performance can be manufactured.",
      "## What happens when the performance slips",
