      "Then the reverse. KFC's UK operation ran out of chicken \u2014 a genuinely absurd failure for a chicken restaurant. They bought a full-page newspaper advert showing an empty bucket with the letters rearranged to spell FCK, and apologised without a single excuse in it. The anger stopped more or less on the spot.",
      "The difference was not budget or cleverness. One of them told the truth about itself at its own expense. The double dropped for a moment and there was a person behind it.",
      "And when it is real from the start, the same network does enormous good \u2014 strangers' medical bills covered by people who will never meet them, causes carried past the gatekeepers who used to decide what counted as news.",
